## 5. Stated limitations and future work (§7 "Limitations", App. B.4, I.3, K)
- The theory is linear and relies on Assumption 3.2. On jannis, per-mode
  identification degrades while the count prediction survives.
- "The criterion is proven in the linear regime, while its extension to images
  is an empirical prediction whose mediating variable is measured after
  predictor equilibration, not at initialisation."
- "the quantitative relation between the initialisation-time budget and the
  effective rank is claimed on tabular data only."
- "The framework governs encoder-side escape given the predictor's state".
- On images, "effective rank is necessary for accuracy without being
  sufficient." Example: at depth 12 on CIFAR-100, SIGReg raises ERank by
  34.5-61.1 with no accuracy change (App. K).
- At deeply subcritical tabular settings ResPred "widens the escape basin
  without guaranteeing a large rank budget: escape there is partial and
  seed-dependent."
- ResPred extends identity bias to attention "by analogy rather than formal
  derivation".
- "µ = 1 is a local initialisation criterion". The ImageNet-1k runs are
  matched-budget pilots, and the full I-JEPA recipe is untested.
- Not covered: the coupled (non-decoupled) derivation ("We do not claim the
  coupled derivation here", App. B.4); the approximate-decoupling version of
  the rank theorems (App. C.6).
- No explicit future-work section. The Conclusion gestures at "theory-driven
  architecture design".

